{"name":"Ametrine Quartz","hex":"#ded1e0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ametrine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A naturally occurring variety of quartz, with zones of purple and yellow or orange."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ametrine"},{"term":"quartz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The most abundant mineral on the earth's surface, of chemical composition silicon dioxide, SiO2. It occurs in a variety of forms, both crystalline and amorphous. Found in every environment.","Crystal meth: methamphetamine hydrochloride."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quartz"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ametrine","blocks":[{"text":"Ametrine, also known as trystine, golden amethyst, or by the trade name bolivianite, is a variety of quartz with alternating zones of purple and yellow-orange coloration. Its name is a portmanteau of amethyst and citrine. While ametrine is commonly referred to as a combination of these two quartz varieties, some sources claim this is not accurate. Almost all commercially available ametrine is mined in Bolivia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Ametrin_from_Bolivia.jpg/330px-Ametrin_from_Bolivia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ametrine"},{"title":"Quartz","blocks":[{"text":"Quartz is a hard mineral composed of silica (silicon dioxide). Its atoms are linked in a continuous framework of SiO4 silicon–oxygen tetrahedra, with each oxygen atom being shared between two tetrahedra, giving an overall chemical formula of SiO2. Therefore, quartz is classified structurally as a framework silicate mineral and compositionally as an oxide mineral. Quartz is the second most common mineral or mineral group in Earth's lithosphere, comprising about 12% by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Quartz_Br%C3%A9sil.jpg/330px-Quartz_Br%C3%A9sil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartz"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Ametrine_cut.jpg/250px-Ametrine_cut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/Ametrine_cut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Ametrine_cut.jpg/250px-Ametrine_cut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ametrine Emerald Cut","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmetrine_cut.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Alpha-quartz%2C_P3_121_and_P3_221.png/500px-Alpha-quartz%2C_P3_121_and_P3_221.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Alpha-quartz%2C_P3_121_and_P3_221.png/1280px-Alpha-quartz%2C_P3_121_and_P3_221.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Alpha-quartz%2C_P3_121_and_P3_221.png/500px-Alpha-quartz%2C_P3_121_and_P3_221.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlpha-quartz%2C_P3_121_and_P3_221.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/00026_40_mm_quartz.jpg/120px-00026_40_mm_quartz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/00026_40_mm_quartz.jpg/250px-00026_40_mm_quartz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/00026_40_mm_quartz.jpg/120px-00026_40_mm_quartz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or